<header><p class="st-kicker">crusader state · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Terra Mariana</h1><p class="st-meta">1207 CE – 1561 CE · capital Riga</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Medieval Livonia, the crusader land dedicated to the Virgin Mary that covered most of modern Latvia and Estonia from the 13th century to 1561.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Terra Mariana grew out of the Livonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-of-riga">Bishop Albert of Riga</a>. In 1207 Albert received his lands as a fief of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a> dedicated the conquered land to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-mother-of-jesus">Virgin Mary</a>, giving it its name. By 1227 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonians">Livonians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latgalians">Latgalians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonians">Estonians</a> had been conquered.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Terra Mariana was never a single state but a patchwork: the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/archbishopric-of-riga">Archbishopric of Riga</a>, the bishoprics of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartu">Dorpat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishopric-of-osel-wiek">Ösel-Wiek</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/courland">Courland</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>, the Danish <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-estonia-1219-1346">Duchy of Estonia</a> (1219-1346), and powerful towns such as Riga and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/reval">Reval</a>. A German-speaking elite of clergy, knights and merchants ruled Latvian, Estonian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonians">Liv</a> peasants, and the towns flourished in Hanseatic trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> spread in the 1520s, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>, begun by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iv-of-russia">Ivan IV of Russia</a> in 1558, broke the region apart. In 1561 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-vilnius-1561">Treaty of Vilnius</a> dissolved the Order's state, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-courland-and-semigallia">Duchy of Courland and Semigallia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-livonia">Duchy of Livonia</a> under Poland-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> took northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-estonia">Estonia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/terra-mariana.jpg" alt="Terra Mariana" width="320" height="347"><figcaption>Image: Termer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Medieval_Livonia_1260.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1207 CE – 1561 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>crusader state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Riga</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Albert of Riga, Wolter von Plettenberg, Gotthard Kettler</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity, Lutheranism from the 1520s</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Low German, Latin, Latvian, Estonian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/latvia">Latvia</a>, <a href="/countries/estonia">Estonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Medieval Livonia, Land of Mary, Marienland</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1384&amp;focus=terra-mariana" aria-label="Terra Mariana on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5200 245 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Terra Mariana lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5520 5